<title>SPAIN: EMU entry to be based on convergence goals-Spain.</title>
<headline>EMU entry to be based on convergence goals-Spain.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said on Monday that nations forming part of European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) will be chosen only on the basis of whether they meet the economic convergence criteria.</p>
<p>&quot;Access to EMU will be given country by country and (on the basis of) the fulfilment of the (Maastricht) Treaty criteria&quot; Rato told a press conference after a meeting with his French counterpart Jean Arthuis.</p>
<p>Rato restated Spain's determination to stick to the convergence criteria and timetable for the euro's launch on January 1, 1999.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
